# Documentation Standards

- Every repo has a README. Internal repos use the INTERNAL template; client repos use the CLIENT template.
- Client-facing docs must be stable, traceable, explainable, and easy to present.
- Never include secrets, internal URLs, internal prompts, or `.cursor` references in client docs.
- Document: purpose, setup (PowerShell), configuration (non-secret), run commands, and architecture.
- Keep setup and run commands accurate and copy-paste ready for Windows PowerShell.
- Note required Azure services and roles where relevant (no secret values).
- Update docs whenever behavior or commands change.
